@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE SCUTTLE PANEL, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* #488 · THE SCUTTLING PANEL. Owner: "we could have a self-destruct option in the ship, like reactor
       overload … in cases where we want to be sure." The third road: it pays NOTHING, which is the only
       reason it can mean anything. No confirmation dialog — the panel states her worth first, and the keys
       are the confirmation. *@
    @* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       #997 wave 4 · THE CARDS THAT BORROWED THE FAMILY'S FOOT — and this is the first of the thirteen.

       Wave 3 put every card ROOTED on `.view-object` on the shell and then wrote down what was left: thirteen
       more cards wearing a `<button class="view-object-close">` on a root of their OWN — the vent boards, the
       operating log, both treasure maps, the lift's car panel, the bar table and the satchel. They took the
       family's button and the family's wording without taking its root, so they were hand-rolling the same
       three lines the other ten had been.

       THEY KEEP THEIR ROOTS. A vent board is a vent board and not a view-object: the shell is the MECHANISM
       and the root class is the IDENTITY, and #995's completeness guard reads that name off this markup as
       typed, so it has to stay a lowercase class attribute exactly where it was. What changes is who draws
       the way out. Same three parameters as wave 3 — `Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare"` (the dismiss stays a DIRECT
       child, which is what `.treasure-map-card > .view-object-close` and every other #735 pin is written
       against), `StopClicks="true"` (the stopPropagation that was typed on the div), and
       `Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"` wired to the page's own close verb, the same one the backdrop behind
       it already calls.

       NOT ONE WORD MOVED, again: "Step away", "Not yet", "Log it", "Back to the board", "Close" and the
       wallet's own keep-it line are the exact strings their own buttons carried, and the two that carried a
       `title` still carry it. Nothing here is standing anywhere either, so wave 2's stranding rule is not
       needed on any of them — every one is a board, a panel, a map or a bag, and putting it down is already
       what its button did.

       THE ONE THAT DID NOT COME. #603's locked door keeps its hand-rolled button, and the guard names it
       with the reason: its way out is one of TWO buttons standing side by side in `.locked-door-actions`,
       beside the brighter "Check your items" the door exists to advertise. Bare draws the dismiss as the
       card's LAST DIRECT CHILD — which is the whole point of the frame — so shelling it would lift that
       button out of the row and drop it on its own line. That is a control moving on the screen. *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="view-object-backdrop" @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseScuttlePanel)">
            <OverlayShell class="vent-board scuttle-panel" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="view-object-close" DismissFace="Step away"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseScuttlePanel)">
                <div class="view-object-title">☢ SCUTTLING PANEL — @scWreck.ShipName.ToUpperInvariant()</div>

                <img class="scuttle-art" src="art/scuttle-panel.jpg" alt=""
                     onerror="this.style.display='none'" />

                <div class="vent-sub">
                    @Scuttle.PriceLine(
                        scWreck.AssessedValueCr,
                        Derelict.Resolve(scWreck, Derelict.SalvageChoice.FileTheReport, scWreck.Cause).CreditsNow)
                </div>

                @if (_scuttleSecondsLeft is { } armedLeft)
                {
                    <div class="vent-message">
                        ☢ RUNNING — @HullVenting.SoakLabel(armedLeft). The way out is the way you came in.
                    </div>
                    <div class="vent-actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm"
                                disabled="@(!Scuttle.CanAbort(armedLeft))"
                                title="@(Scuttle.CanAbort(armedLeft) ? "" : Scuttle.PastRecallLine)"
                                @onclick="AbortTheOverload">
                            🔑 Back the keys out
                        </button>
                        @if (!Scuttle.CanAbort(armedLeft))
                        {
                            <div class="vent-refusal">@Scuttle.PastRecallLine</div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="vent-actions">
                        @foreach (Scuttle.Method m in ScuttleMethods())
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger btn-sm"
                                    title="@($"Takes {Scuttle.Speed(m)}. Nobody pays you to be sure.")"
                                    @onclick="ArmTheOverload">
                                ☢ Turn both keys — reactor overload
                            </button>
                        }
                        @* The methods this hull cannot do, and WHY. A greyed control that does not say why
                           is a bug wearing a tooltip's clothes. *@
                        @foreach (Scuttle.Method m in System.Enum.GetValues<Scuttle.Method>())
                        {
                            @if (!ScuttleMethods().Contains(m))
                            {
                                <div class="vent-refusal">@Scuttle.Refusal(m, scWreck.Cause)</div>
                            }
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    // ── WHAT THESE PARAMETERS ARE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // #251 item 1 · Every [Parameter] below carries a member of the page under THE MEMBER'S OWN NAME —
    // a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate with its own signature, a variable the
    // page's `@if` binds arrives under the name the `@if` gave it. That is the whole trick of this
    // refactor: it is what let the markup above move out of Map.razor without a single character of it
    // changing, and what lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as they read it
    // when it lived in the page. A parameter that needs saying more than that says it on its own line.

    [Parameter] public double? _scuttleSecondsLeft { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Action AbortTheOverload { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action ArmTheOverload { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Action CloseScuttlePanel { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Func<IReadOnlyList<Scuttle.Method>> ScuttleMethods { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Derelict.Wreck scWreck { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
